Ms. Thackston,<br />
<br />
The Division has today filed a notice withdrawing Count II of the order ins=
tituting proceedings in its entirety, together with paragraphs 14 through 2=
2 of the order, which contain the allegation that the staff obtained a writ=
ten undertaking from your client at the conclusion of examination 2012-0331=
 and the allegation that the undertaking was lost in the 2016 migration. Th=
e Division does not intend to seek leave to amend and will not assert the a=
llegation in any other form.<br />
<br />
You are entitled to know the basis, so I will state it rather than leave it=
 to be inferred.<br />
<br />
The Division searched the Commission's electronic mail journal archive, whi=
ch retains every message sent or received on the Commission's messaging sys=
tem with its attachments and from which nothing has been destroyed since 20=
11. The search covered the mailboxes of the examination staff and, on a sec=
ond pass, of the regional director's office, over the period January 2012 t=
hrough December 2014, full text including the contents of attachments. It r=
eturned no deficiency letter, no undertaking and no corrective action commi=
tment concerning your client. The Division separately restored the complete=
 examination work paper set from the retired examination system. The work p=
apers record that no deficiencies were identified and that the examination =
was closed on that basis.<br />
<br />
In short, the Division looked in the place where the document would be if i=
t existed, and the document is not there, because it never existed. Your le=
tter of September 5 was correct.<br />
<br />
Counts I and III proceed on the existing schedule. The Division's supplemen=
tal production, including the search scope memorandum and the results index=
 for both searches, is served with this letter so that you have the negativ=
e result in the same form you would have had a positive one.<br />
<br />
Warrick Osunde<br />
Senior Counsel, Division of Enforcement